# Scratch output dirs stay on disk; `results/` (the committed JSONL evidence) is re-included.
#
# THIS FILE NO LONGER OWNS THE BIOME FENCE (#2299, 2026-09-13). It used to, as a documented SIDE EFFECT:
# biome runs with `vcs.useIgnoreFile: true`, reads nested ignore files, and does not honour their
# negations, so `*/` took the whole directory out of biome's scope. That was invisible to every instrument
# and the EDIT HOOK disagreed with it — `tooling/biome.edit.jsonc`'s `experimentalScannerIgnores` suppresses
# nested ignore-file discovery, so the hook linted these files and reported 15 errors on `_kit.ts` that the
# shipping gate never saw. The fence is now an explicit `!scripts/probes/openrouter` in `biome.json`'s
# `files.includes`, which `biome.edit.jsonc` inherits by `extends`, and its reason plus END CONDITION are
# data in `tests/tooling/biome-scripts-probe-scope.int.test.ts`. Change the fence THERE, not here.
*/
!results/
